            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0218" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6–3047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-30">June 30,
                        1947</date>.<lb/>[Received June 30—5:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>121. Special press release, June 30, states Nationalist troops moving northwards
                    from Mukden reached Ssupingkai at 9 a.m. today and joined forces with besieged
                    garrison in southwestern suburb of city.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking as 207, repeated Department as 121 and Changchun as 101.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
